WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.490 --> 00:07.590
In that scenario with Aaliyah and David, she’s very fortunate to be able to have access to a board member to ask for that kind of advice.

2
00:07.970 --> 00:10.270
Most of us don’t have that. So what can we do?

3
00:11.050 --> 00:15.940
I actually suggest: just ring a friend, ask a colleague to help you out with some of these things.

4
00:16.360 --> 00:21.830
Just like a good conversation doesn’t happen on its own, good delivery doesn’t happen on its own either.

5
00:22.500 --> 00:27.200
And so there are lots of tips and tricks, where it can be about the basic things like room setup

6
00:27.530 --> 00:35.010
or how you appear on the screen. But then it’s also about practicing some of that vocal delivery and trying on some of those different styles,

7
00:35.460 --> 00:41.190
things that might be a little bit out of your comfort zone. Some people like practicing in front of a mirror.

8
00:41.610 --> 00:46.110
Other people like practicing in front of a friend or a colleague who can give them some feedback,

9
00:47.110 --> 00:51.590
because sometimes we’re just not aware of how we appear on screen or in a different setting.

10
00:52.010 --> 00:57.350
And what might feel awkward to us might actually be really impactful or energizing to someone else.

11
00:58.340 --> 01:07.300
Another great resource for practicing this skill can be a local chapter of Toastmasters, or even delivering an address at a local community group or place of worship.

